    <GaugingStation location="Heighington" name="Heighington Beck" number="30013">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Crump weir gauging a slow responding limestone catchment with significant artificial influences during summer.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Theoretical calibration but drowning expected at high flows. One rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Crump profile weir 3.51m wide.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Very slow responding. Summer low flows may be heavily influenced by gw abstraction for irrigation.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Permeable geology - almost entirely limestone, with minimal superficial deposits. Predominantly rural, mixed farming but with some urban development.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">GI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED. Weir remains modular." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Most high flows remain modular. Rating fits well to available gaugings." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
